**The composed annotation**
- `@SpringBootApplication` = `@Configuration` + `@EnableAutoConfiguration` + `@ComponentScan`
- Each component can be applied separately when full Boot semantics aren't wanted

**`@Configuration`**
- Marks the class as a source of bean definitions
- Methods annotated `@Bean` register Spring beans
- The class itself is also a Spring bean

**`@EnableAutoConfiguration`**
- Triggers `AutoConfigurationImportSelector` to scan `META-INF/spring/AutoConfiguration.imports`
- Each listed configuration class is conditionally evaluated against the classpath and existing beans

**`@ComponentScan`**
- Scans the package of the annotated class and subpackages for `@Component`, `@Service`, `@Repository`, `@Controller`
- Default scan root is the package containing `@SpringBootApplication`

```java
@SpringBootApplication
public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(App.class, args);
    }
}

@Configuration
@EnableAutoConfiguration
@ComponentScan(basePackages = "com.example.web")
public class CustomApp { }
```

**Dependencies**
- `spring-cloud-starter-netflix-eureka-client` — registers with Eureka discovery
- `spring-cloud-starter-config` — pulls config from Spring Cloud Config Server at startup
- `spring-cloud-starter-loadbalancer` — client-side load balancing across discovered instances

**bootstrap.yml — loaded before application.yml so Config Server is contacted first**

```yaml
spring:
  application:
    name: order-service
  config:
    import: "configserver:http://config-server:8888"
  cloud:
    discovery:
      enabled: true
eureka:
  client:
    service-url:
      defaultZone: http://eureka:8761/eureka/
```

**Calling another service by logical name**

```java
@Configuration
public class HttpConfig {
    @Bean
    @LoadBalanced
    public RestClient.Builder restClientBuilder() {
        return RestClient.builder();
    }
}

@Service
public class PaymentClient {
    private final RestClient http;

    public PaymentClient(RestClient.Builder b) {
        this.http = b.baseUrl("http://payment-service").build();
    }

    public PaymentResult charge(ChargeRequest req) {
        return http.post().uri("/charge")
            .body(req).retrieve().body(PaymentResult.class);
    }
}
```

**Operational notes**
- The `@LoadBalanced` `RestClient.Builder` resolves `payment-service` via discovery and load-balances across instances
- No hardcoded URLs; instances are discovered dynamically
- Add `spring-cloud-starter-circuitbreaker-resilience4j` to wrap calls in a circuit breaker
